# Secure Files

Two layers — do not mix them:

| Path | Access | Allowed types |
|------|--------|---------------|
| `/uploads/*` | Public | `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.webp` only |
| `/api/files/:filename` | Auth + `canAccessFile()` | PDFs, medical docs, attachments |

❌ Never expose PDFs or medical documents via `/uploads`.
❌ Never use `<a href="/uploads/...">` for sensitive files in frontend.

✅ Frontend: use `openSecureFile()` from `src/utils/openSecureFile.ts`.

Reference: `docs/FILE-SECURITY.md`, `CLAUDE.md`.
